1
00:01:33,680 --> 00:01:37,120
We're all going to get rich together!

2
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:39,800
<i>Hurry. I think he's starting to catch on.</i>

3
00:01:39,880 --> 00:01:40,960
Wow,

4
00:01:41,040 --> 00:01:43,120
so this is the control room.
I've been looking for it.

5
00:01:43,200 --> 00:01:44,280
Is there a problem?

6
00:01:44,360 --> 00:01:47,320
<i>There's a problem on stage.</i>
<i>The stage video has been hacked.</i>

7
00:01:47,400 --> 00:01:49,200
Haven't you learned anything?

8
00:01:49,280 --> 00:01:52,560
When you mess with us,
you've got to think of everything.

9
00:01:52,640 --> 00:01:54,280
Then you all have to pay too.

10
00:01:54,360 --> 00:01:57,320
For the past 13 years,
while you were running in panic,

11
00:01:57,400 --> 00:01:58,360
you didn't even know

12
00:01:58,440 --> 00:02:00,840
Hong spent all the money herself.

13
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:01,800
You idiots.

14
00:02:01,880 --> 00:02:05,440
Now we don't know what was real

15
00:02:05,520 --> 00:02:06,680
and what was a lie.

16
00:02:06,760 --> 00:02:09,400
Why didn't you just tell her the truth
that you know her dad?

17
00:02:09,479 --> 00:02:10,840
What do you want me to say?

18
00:02:10,919 --> 00:02:13,840
<i>"Sorry I had a part</i>
<i>in your dad's disappearance."</i>

19
00:02:13,920 --> 00:02:14,960
<i>You want me to say that?</i>

20
00:02:18,840 --> 00:02:19,720
I'm not going in.

21
00:02:21,640 --> 00:02:24,040
He told you to go in, so go.

22
00:02:24,640 --> 00:02:25,640
Hey.

23
00:02:26,240 --> 00:02:27,240
What the hell is this?

24
00:02:32,800 --> 00:02:35,040
Go back, Koh. Your job here is done.

25
00:02:35,800 --> 00:02:39,160
I thought we were just here to talk.
What are you planning to do, James?

26
00:02:42,600 --> 00:02:44,280
I told you to go back.

27
00:02:45,160 --> 00:02:46,320
This has nothing to do with you.

28
00:03:02,880 --> 00:03:03,920
Leave.

29
00:03:29,040 --> 00:03:30,080
Run, bro!

30
00:03:30,960 --> 00:03:31,960
Go.

31
00:03:51,880 --> 00:03:53,720
Run, Aek! Run!

32
00:04:24,160 --> 00:04:25,560
Run.

33
00:04:36,360 --> 00:04:40,120
<i>The last thing I saw</i>
<i>was Aek trying to get away.</i>

34
00:04:43,480 --> 00:04:47,720
But I don't know if he made it or not.

35
00:04:49,080 --> 00:04:51,640
You were shot that badly.
How did you even survive?

36
00:04:52,760 --> 00:04:55,000
The doctor said the bullet
barely missed my heart.

37
00:04:56,960 --> 00:04:59,320
After I woke up, they hit me
with a bunch of charges.

38
00:05:00,400 --> 00:05:02,920
Shooting a cop and extortion.

39
00:05:07,400 --> 00:05:10,680
Hey, Koh, look on the bright side.
If you hadn't gone to prison,

40
00:05:10,760 --> 00:05:13,480
we never would've met, right?

41
00:05:13,560 --> 00:05:14,880
But still…

42
00:05:15,440 --> 00:05:17,680
If I hadn't taken Aek there that day,

43
00:05:19,320 --> 00:05:21,800
Risa wouldn't have ended up like this.

44
00:05:41,960 --> 00:05:43,320
Is Mr. Louis here?

45
00:05:52,160 --> 00:05:53,840
It's not that complicated.

46
00:05:53,920 --> 00:05:57,120
If any checkpoint gives you trouble,
just pay them off.

47
00:05:57,200 --> 00:06:00,200
Let's do this. I'll pay you double.

48
00:06:00,280 --> 00:06:02,560
But I want a 10% cut. Okay?

49
00:06:09,880 --> 00:06:13,000
Go discuss it with the General.

50
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:20,840
Is something wrong, Deputy James?

51
00:06:20,920 --> 00:06:22,800
What brings you here?

52
00:06:25,240 --> 00:06:27,160
Mam Yollada died in prison.

53
00:06:28,360 --> 00:06:30,480
And right now, the police

54
00:06:30,560 --> 00:06:32,800
don't believe it was a suicide.

55
00:06:33,400 --> 00:06:36,240
Which police? You?

56
00:06:45,080 --> 00:06:46,240
Hey, listen.

57
00:06:47,000 --> 00:06:48,920
I checked the records.

58
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:51,400
Even if your name

59
00:06:51,480 --> 00:06:53,200
wasn't on the visitor log,

60
00:06:53,920 --> 00:06:57,800
you shouldn't be showing up
in places like that without my knowledge.

61
00:06:58,320 --> 00:07:00,400
Same thing with Boss Kluay.

62
00:07:01,520 --> 00:07:04,360
Anyway, I'll take care of the Mam case.

63
00:07:05,600 --> 00:07:08,680
Some things I'd rather handle myself.

64
00:07:11,280 --> 00:07:12,640
Then next time,

65
00:07:13,480 --> 00:07:16,080
don't leave any evidence behind.

66
00:07:22,720 --> 00:07:26,280
I've already replaced
all the CCTV hard drives.

67
00:07:27,440 --> 00:07:29,080
Because I know

68
00:07:29,160 --> 00:07:31,760
you'll clean up the rest for me.

69
00:07:37,920 --> 00:07:40,760
I want you to deal with these guys.

70
00:07:42,640 --> 00:07:45,800
They're the ones who messed
with Kluay and Mam.

71
00:07:48,880 --> 00:07:50,760
CIVIL REGISTRATION CERTIFICATE

72
00:07:50,840 --> 00:07:51,680
CIVIL REGISTRATION CERTIFICATE

73
00:07:56,080 --> 00:07:58,280
CIVIL REGISTRATION CERTIFICATE
KONGKIAT KAMNERDRAT

74
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:04,000
I know this guy very well.

75
00:08:07,640 --> 00:08:11,120
And I know exactly
how to lure the others into a trap.

76
00:08:11,880 --> 00:08:16,600
Good. When I become an MP,

77
00:08:17,480 --> 00:08:19,000
I won't forget you.

78
00:08:23,160 --> 00:08:26,240
CIVIL REGISTRATION CERTIFICATE
KONGKIAT KAMNERDRAT

79
00:08:27,120 --> 00:08:29,760
Relax, man. There's a solution
to every problem.

80
00:08:30,680 --> 00:08:31,840
Why are you so stressed?

81
00:08:36,039 --> 00:08:37,360
-Koh.
-Huh?

82
00:08:40,159 --> 00:08:41,159
Why is my shop open?

83
00:08:43,280 --> 00:08:45,760
-Did Sis Hong come down and unlock it?
-No.

84
00:08:45,840 --> 00:08:49,800
Angpao said Risa was taking Sis Hong
to the hospital for a checkup.

85
00:08:50,360 --> 00:08:51,760
Maybe she's worried
she has liver cirrhosis.

86
00:08:53,520 --> 00:08:54,920
-Let's go.
-Hey.

87
00:08:55,720 --> 00:08:57,640
-What?
-Don't tell me…

88
00:08:58,960 --> 00:09:00,560
Risa came here to settle things with me.

89
00:09:00,640 --> 00:09:03,000
Good. Then I'll wait outside.

90
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:04,360
You two need to talk.

91
00:09:04,440 --> 00:09:06,120
Looks like you've got a lot to discuss.
I'm heading out.

92
00:09:06,200 --> 00:09:08,320
-Hey, Chen, wait.
-Go work things out.

93
00:09:08,400 --> 00:09:10,000
-Chen!
-Talk it through properly, man.

94
00:09:14,280 --> 00:09:15,880
Geez.

95
00:09:37,600 --> 00:09:39,880
Hey, Captain Koh.

96
00:09:42,880 --> 00:09:43,840
How've you been?

97
00:09:49,760 --> 00:09:51,280
James.

98
00:09:52,600 --> 00:09:53,440
What do you want?

99
00:09:54,480 --> 00:09:57,760
Hey. It's been a long time.

100
00:09:58,560 --> 00:10:00,600
Can you speak a little more politely?

101
00:10:03,560 --> 00:10:06,040
Don't think I don't know

102
00:10:06,120 --> 00:10:10,240
what you've been up to
since you got out of prison.

103
00:10:12,840 --> 00:10:15,000
I didn't mess with you before

104
00:10:15,640 --> 00:10:18,840
because you never crossed the line
or caused me any trouble.

105
00:10:21,960 --> 00:10:23,000
What are you talking about?

106
00:10:26,920 --> 00:10:28,520
Stop playing dumb.

107
00:10:30,960 --> 00:10:34,480
Your group went after
Boss Kluay and Mam Yollada.

108
00:10:35,480 --> 00:10:37,760
Someone's not happy about that.

109
00:10:38,360 --> 00:10:41,160
So they sent me to deal with it.

110
00:10:46,480 --> 00:10:47,600
Tell me.

111
00:10:48,800 --> 00:10:50,360
Your group members,

112
00:10:51,160 --> 00:10:52,440
where are they?

113
00:10:53,120 --> 00:10:56,360
And who is this Admin guy?

114
00:11:06,280 --> 00:11:09,640
Yeah. Since you've already tricked her
into going to the hospital,

115
00:11:09,720 --> 00:11:11,960
find a way to get her checked.

116
00:11:13,240 --> 00:11:15,480
Get Mungkorn to help figure it out.

117
00:11:16,120 --> 00:11:19,680
Anyway, I've got something
to take care of.

118
00:11:19,760 --> 00:11:21,960
I'll catch up with you
after I'm done. Yeah.

119
00:11:26,840 --> 00:11:30,040
I don't know who Admin is.
He never reveals himself.

120
00:11:32,400 --> 00:11:35,960
Koh, if you cooperate with me,

121
00:11:36,040 --> 00:11:37,840
I'll let you go.

122
00:11:40,960 --> 00:11:44,480
How can I trust you
not to betray me again?

123
00:11:47,840 --> 00:11:51,640
Do you really have
a better option right now?

124
00:11:52,240 --> 00:11:54,800
You know, for someone at my level,

125
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:57,360
finding all of you

126
00:11:57,440 --> 00:11:58,720
isn't that difficult.

127
00:12:00,400 --> 00:12:03,360
But I'm being generous
because back then, you and your mother

128
00:12:03,440 --> 00:12:06,480
used to be servants in my house.

129
00:12:07,480 --> 00:12:09,000
So I'm giving you a chance.

130
00:12:14,720 --> 00:12:16,560
If you mess with my mother,

131
00:12:17,600 --> 00:12:18,800
you're dead.

132
00:12:22,480 --> 00:12:23,920
I wouldn't do that, Koh.

133
00:12:24,920 --> 00:12:28,120
But if you don't cooperate, who knows?

134
00:12:33,400 --> 00:12:37,080
I'll give you a day to think about it.

135
00:12:38,640 --> 00:12:40,280
Think carefully.

136
00:12:42,440 --> 00:12:43,800
You son of a servant.

137
00:12:57,120 --> 00:12:58,160
Wait.

138
00:13:05,760 --> 00:13:07,320
I've got one more question.

139
00:13:11,080 --> 00:13:12,200
Where's Aek now?

140
00:13:15,960 --> 00:13:17,840
Why are you suddenly asking about him?

141
00:13:18,480 --> 00:13:19,520
Feeling guilty?

142
00:13:20,320 --> 00:13:21,600
Want to apologize to him?

143
00:13:24,480 --> 00:13:25,840
Can you just tell me?

144
00:13:27,080 --> 00:13:29,520
-Please.
-You're actually begging now?

145
00:13:31,960 --> 00:13:34,880
The last thing I heard about Aek

146
00:13:35,480 --> 00:13:37,600
was that Mr. Louis captured him.

147
00:13:40,640 --> 00:13:43,400
-Which Louis?
-Mr. Louis from the Hyena Group,

148
00:13:43,480 --> 00:13:46,760
the owner of Hyena Pub,
who Aek used to work for.

149
00:13:46,840 --> 00:13:49,400
You went there to collect protection money
five years ago.

150
00:13:52,480 --> 00:13:54,720
Honestly, I don't know

151
00:13:54,800 --> 00:13:58,160
what Aek did to him,
but it must've been serious.

152
00:13:59,240 --> 00:14:00,960
And where can I find Louis?

153
00:14:01,040 --> 00:14:03,680
The Hyena Group operates in Poipet.

154
00:14:41,560 --> 00:14:44,480
Hello. What's up, Koh? You've been
talking to her for a long time.

155
00:14:44,560 --> 00:14:46,920
Chen, call everyone and tell them

156
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:48,520
the police are after us.

157
00:14:49,280 --> 00:14:50,120
Wait.

158
00:14:50,200 --> 00:14:52,120
Hey. What happened, Koh?

159
00:14:52,200 --> 00:14:56,120
James, the cop who used me to arrest Aek,

160
00:14:56,200 --> 00:14:57,320
was at your shop.

161
00:14:58,720 --> 00:15:01,160
-What?
<i>-Hurry back and meet me at the shop.</i>

162
00:15:01,240 --> 00:15:02,200
Now.

163
00:15:13,360 --> 00:15:15,120
You know my dad, don't you?

164
00:15:20,600 --> 00:15:21,560
I heard everything.

165
00:15:24,560 --> 00:15:26,480
Why didn't you ever tell me about this?

166
00:15:30,160 --> 00:15:32,960
Risa, I'm sorry.

167
00:15:33,040 --> 00:15:35,160
But don't think about that right now.

168
00:15:35,240 --> 00:15:37,320
The police are after us.

169
00:15:37,400 --> 00:15:39,880
You need to go somewhere safe and hide.

170
00:15:42,600 --> 00:15:44,480
Don't act like you're worried about me.

171
00:16:12,080 --> 00:16:16,560
Sis, we're already at the hospital.
You should let the doctor examine you.

172
00:16:16,640 --> 00:16:20,120
Tell me honestly. Who came up with
the idea of tricking me into coming here?

173
00:16:20,200 --> 00:16:23,040
Risa saw how much
you've been drinking lately.

174
00:16:23,120 --> 00:16:26,240
She was worried, so she wanted you
to get a checkup.

175
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:28,360
What?

176
00:16:29,720 --> 00:16:30,760
Sis!

177
00:16:32,960 --> 00:16:34,840
Geez.

178
00:16:34,920 --> 00:16:35,840
Hello, Ris.

179
00:16:35,920 --> 00:16:38,920
-Angpao, where are you right now?
<i>-I'm on my way to Chen's shop.</i>

180
00:16:39,000 --> 00:16:41,480
Why? What's going on?

181
00:16:41,560 --> 00:16:44,840
Don't come back here.
Take her to the base and meet me there.

182
00:16:44,920 --> 00:16:46,320
The police are after us right now.

183
00:16:46,400 --> 00:16:47,560
What?

184
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:50,040
They're after us?

185
00:16:50,120 --> 00:16:51,320
How do you even know that?

186
00:16:51,400 --> 00:16:55,000
Just get back here quickly.
I'll explain later. That's it.

187
00:17:13,079 --> 00:17:15,480
Why aren't those two old men answering?

188
00:17:19,560 --> 00:17:21,319
Don't tell me they've been arrested.

189
00:17:21,960 --> 00:17:23,800
How did the police even find out?

190
00:17:25,839 --> 00:17:28,680
Hey, don't tell me Admin tricked us

191
00:17:29,480 --> 00:17:31,960
and made us take the fall for him.

192
00:17:32,560 --> 00:17:34,320
Why would he do that?

193
00:17:35,400 --> 00:17:39,000
If it were Admin, we would've
been arrested a long time ago.

194
00:17:45,320 --> 00:17:46,360
Ris.

195
00:17:48,920 --> 00:17:50,080
Are you okay?

196
00:17:51,880 --> 00:17:53,080
I'm fine. Nothing's wrong.

197
00:17:58,320 --> 00:18:00,720
Who is it? Gao and Yak?

198
00:18:00,800 --> 00:18:03,640
No, it's Chen.

199
00:18:07,320 --> 00:18:10,000
-Hello.
-Are you all safe?

200
00:18:10,080 --> 00:18:14,120
Okay. We'll head to the base
and meet you there.

201
00:18:17,040 --> 00:18:18,400
Alright.

202
00:18:19,240 --> 00:18:20,520
Hey, Koh, wait.

203
00:18:22,160 --> 00:18:23,040
Where are you going?

204
00:18:24,040 --> 00:18:25,080
I'm going to Poipet.

205
00:18:25,160 --> 00:18:28,080
Huh? You're going to Poipet right now?

206
00:18:28,160 --> 00:18:30,360
How can you go?

207
00:18:30,440 --> 00:18:32,480
I already told everyone
we'd meet at the base.

208
00:18:32,560 --> 00:18:35,520
Chen, I'm going alone.

209
00:18:37,600 --> 00:18:40,360
Are you crazy, Koh? Do you know
how dangerous it is right now?

210
00:18:40,440 --> 00:18:41,760
Exactly.

211
00:18:41,840 --> 00:18:44,760
It's dangerous. That's why I want you
to stay and look after them.

212
00:18:44,840 --> 00:18:46,360
Especially Risa.

213
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:50,080
Don't let her do anything reckless.
Understand?

214
00:18:50,960 --> 00:18:52,160
Koh.

215
00:18:53,920 --> 00:18:55,320
I'm not letting you go.

216
00:18:57,680 --> 00:19:00,040
This might be my last chance

217
00:19:00,560 --> 00:19:03,840
to make things right.

218
00:19:08,960 --> 00:19:10,320
Take care of things for me.

219
00:19:40,320 --> 00:19:42,720
<i>The last thing I heard about Aek</i>

220
00:19:42,800 --> 00:19:45,040
<i>was that Mr. Louis captured him.</i>

221
00:19:45,120 --> 00:19:46,120
<i>Which Louis?</i>

222
00:19:46,800 --> 00:19:50,200
Mr. Louis from the Hyena Group,
the owner of Hyena Pub,

223
00:19:50,280 --> 00:19:52,560
who Aek used to work for.

224
00:19:52,640 --> 00:19:54,840
You went there to collect
protection money five years ago.

225
00:19:57,720 --> 00:19:59,120
Hyena Group?

226
00:20:19,560 --> 00:20:20,480
Hey, Ris.

227
00:20:21,280 --> 00:20:23,440
Hungry? Want something to eat?

228
00:20:23,960 --> 00:20:25,840
I'm okay, thanks.

229
00:20:25,920 --> 00:20:28,280
Okay. I'll take this inside to the others.

230
00:20:29,880 --> 00:20:30,760
Angpao, wait.

231
00:20:33,840 --> 00:20:37,240
I need your help with something.

232
00:20:45,840 --> 00:20:48,280
I tried to look up
this company's information,

233
00:20:48,880 --> 00:20:50,440
but when I got in,

234
00:20:50,520 --> 00:20:53,360
all I found were ad pop-ups.

235
00:20:53,440 --> 00:20:55,880
"Income 25,000-30,000 per month,

236
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:58,240
with free accommodation.

237
00:20:58,320 --> 00:20:59,720
No experience required."

238
00:21:00,440 --> 00:21:04,200
So sketchy. What kind of job is this?
It's obviously illegal.

239
00:21:04,280 --> 00:21:06,080
I want to know

240
00:21:06,160 --> 00:21:08,720
where this website's domain is registered.

241
00:21:10,240 --> 00:21:12,080
And where its latest update

242
00:21:12,160 --> 00:21:13,560
was uploaded from.

243
00:21:13,640 --> 00:21:15,960
Can you help me find the IP address?

244
00:21:23,480 --> 00:21:26,720
-Here it is. Found it.
-Where?

245
00:21:29,200 --> 00:21:30,280
Poipet.

246
00:21:33,000 --> 00:21:35,400
The Hyena Group operates in Poipet.

247
00:21:57,880 --> 00:22:01,920
Hello. Yeah, I've arrived.
How are you guys? Are you all safe?

248
00:22:02,000 --> 00:22:03,600
Hey, everyone's safe.

249
00:22:03,680 --> 00:22:06,280
We're laying low at the Admin base.

250
00:22:06,360 --> 00:22:07,200
<i>Huh?</i>

251
00:22:07,280 --> 00:22:10,560
At that abandoned warehouse by the pier?
You can actually stay there?

252
00:22:10,640 --> 00:22:12,600
We didn't really want to.

253
00:22:15,520 --> 00:22:18,200
Sis Hong is waiting
for the two old men here.

254
00:22:20,240 --> 00:22:22,880
And what about Risa?

255
00:22:25,000 --> 00:22:28,320
She's safe. Don't worry, Koh.
She's here with us.

256
00:22:29,160 --> 00:22:30,720
How about you?

257
00:22:31,400 --> 00:22:33,800
I know someone local.
I'll try to dig around a bit.

258
00:22:34,320 --> 00:22:36,320
Hey, can you trust him?

259
00:22:36,400 --> 00:22:38,560
Make sure you're careful
about who you rely on.

260
00:22:38,640 --> 00:22:41,720
<i>Yeah, I trust him.</i>
<i>I've known him since he was a cop.</i>

261
00:22:41,800 --> 00:22:44,640
He's left the police
and is working in Cambodia now.

262
00:22:45,400 --> 00:22:46,560
<i>He used to be my subordinate.</i>

263
00:22:47,320 --> 00:22:48,160
That's it for now.

264
00:22:48,240 --> 00:22:49,840
<i>Alright. Stay safe, man.</i>

265
00:22:49,920 --> 00:22:50,960
Yeah.

266
00:23:00,720 --> 00:23:02,640
Hey, Mungkorn.

267
00:23:02,720 --> 00:23:04,720
Why are you standing there?
Bring the plates. The eggs are ready.

268
00:23:04,800 --> 00:23:06,040
Okay.

269
00:23:07,880 --> 00:23:09,120
-Nice and crispy.
-Here you go.

270
00:23:09,720 --> 00:23:11,080
Thank you.

271
00:23:13,440 --> 00:23:15,240
-Chen.
-Yes?

272
00:23:15,320 --> 00:23:17,040
You never said Koh went to Cambodia.

273
00:23:25,320 --> 00:23:30,400
Oh, Koh just went there
to scout things out.

274
00:23:31,000 --> 00:23:33,320
In case the police come after us,

275
00:23:33,400 --> 00:23:35,720
we can flee there.

276
00:23:37,760 --> 00:23:39,520
Yeah.

277
00:23:39,600 --> 00:23:41,000
Okay.

278
00:23:41,760 --> 00:23:44,680
Good, the plates are here.
I'll fry some more eggs.

279
00:23:50,560 --> 00:23:52,000
Angpao.

280
00:23:52,080 --> 00:23:55,800
Is the rice I asked you to cook ready yet?
I sent you to cook it ages ago.

281
00:23:56,400 --> 00:23:57,520
It's ready.

282
00:23:58,520 --> 00:23:59,480
-Alright.
-It's done.

283
00:23:59,560 --> 00:24:01,400
That took a while.

284
00:24:07,760 --> 00:24:11,240
I told you to cook rice,
not go buy it at the supermarket.

285
00:24:11,320 --> 00:24:12,640
You went and bought this?

286
00:24:12,720 --> 00:24:13,800
Of course, Chen.

287
00:24:14,400 --> 00:24:17,800
Hey, this isn't scout camp.

288
00:24:17,880 --> 00:24:20,360
I can't wake up every day

289
00:24:20,440 --> 00:24:23,160
to wash rice and start a fire.

290
00:24:23,240 --> 00:24:24,760
And most importantly,

291
00:24:25,560 --> 00:24:28,240
after everyone's done eating,
I still have to wash the pot.

292
00:24:28,320 --> 00:24:30,240
Buying it is easier.

293
00:24:30,320 --> 00:24:32,880
I get it, but it's dangerous.

294
00:24:32,960 --> 00:24:34,840
When you buy stuff at the supermarket,

295
00:24:34,920 --> 00:24:37,280
you never know whether
there are CCTV cameras there or not.

296
00:24:38,200 --> 00:24:39,320
Don't worry, Chen.

297
00:24:39,400 --> 00:24:42,120
I've watched a lot of movies. Look.

298
00:24:45,840 --> 00:24:47,440
I got it from a disguise expert.

299
00:24:47,520 --> 00:24:49,160
Here, see?

300
00:24:49,920 --> 00:24:53,760
Perfect disguise. Plus, I used cash.

301
00:24:53,840 --> 00:24:56,640
No way to trace me. No evidence.

302
00:25:10,920 --> 00:25:11,960
Sis Hong.

303
00:25:12,800 --> 00:25:13,920
Let's go eat.

304
00:25:14,520 --> 00:25:15,840
I'm not hungry.

305
00:25:18,000 --> 00:25:20,920
Has Gao still not picked up?

306
00:25:26,720 --> 00:25:30,520
Forget it. Whatever happens, happens.

307
00:25:36,120 --> 00:25:39,200
Let's go eat. At least we'll have
the energy to enjoy ourselves.

308
00:25:43,960 --> 00:25:44,920
What's there to eat?

309
00:25:45,720 --> 00:25:47,240
-Plenty.
-Yes!

310
00:25:48,960 --> 00:25:50,640
Do I look like him?

311
00:25:50,720 --> 00:25:52,400
Sis Hong.

312
00:25:52,480 --> 00:25:54,920
Have you seen Risa?

313
00:25:55,000 --> 00:25:57,520
I saw her briefly this morning.

314
00:26:10,480 --> 00:26:13,040
I was going to ask where she was going,
but I didn't get the chance.

315
00:26:15,320 --> 00:26:17,120
Did she tell you where she was going?

316
00:26:18,160 --> 00:26:19,000
No, she didn't.

317
00:26:21,360 --> 00:26:23,320
Where did she go?

318
00:26:47,360 --> 00:26:48,720
MUNGKORN

319
00:27:00,200 --> 00:27:03,200
SA KAEO 10 KM, KABINBURI 42 KM

320
00:27:05,000 --> 00:27:06,080
Still not answering.

321
00:27:07,800 --> 00:27:09,040
Try again.

322
00:27:11,960 --> 00:27:15,480
Don't tell me she already applied.

323
00:27:16,800 --> 00:27:18,320
Applied for what?

324
00:27:18,400 --> 00:27:19,800
Last night,

325
00:27:20,680 --> 00:27:24,640
Ris asked me to look up information
about Hyena Group in Poipet.

326
00:27:25,400 --> 00:27:27,000
I don't know why she was searching for it,

327
00:27:27,080 --> 00:27:30,520
but Hyena Group
is definitely an illegal operation.

328
00:27:30,600 --> 00:27:33,680
Pao, pull it up for me right now.

329
00:27:39,200 --> 00:27:40,280
Here, this one.

330
00:27:40,360 --> 00:27:41,240
URGENT! NOW HIRING
FOR ONLINE MARKETING POSITIONS

331
00:27:41,320 --> 00:27:45,520
This looks just like those scam ads
for call-center jobs.

332
00:27:47,040 --> 00:27:51,360
Hey, hold on. So Risa was tricked?

333
00:27:53,160 --> 00:27:55,440
I'm screwed again.

334
00:27:56,040 --> 00:27:57,080
Chen.

335
00:27:58,080 --> 00:27:59,040
Is something going on?

336
00:27:59,120 --> 00:28:01,720
No, nothing at all.

337
00:28:03,480 --> 00:28:07,520
Wait. Is this about Koh going to Cambodia?

338
00:28:09,840 --> 00:28:10,760
Chen.

339
00:28:11,480 --> 00:28:14,640
What do you know? Tell me everything now.

340
00:28:35,120 --> 00:28:38,520
Once the door opens,
everyone run into the forest. Got it?

341
00:28:38,600 --> 00:28:40,040
Hey, why do we have to run?

342
00:28:40,120 --> 00:28:41,440
We're here to apply for a job.

343
00:28:41,520 --> 00:28:44,920
This is way too suspicious.
I'm out. I don't want to do this anymore.

344
00:28:46,880 --> 00:28:49,160
You do what you're told.

345
00:29:01,000 --> 00:29:02,240
Get out! Move!

346
00:29:02,320 --> 00:29:03,800
Get out now!

347
00:30:36,680 --> 00:30:38,600
We're here. Keep up.

348
00:30:50,560 --> 00:30:51,760
We've arrived, boss.

349
00:31:11,280 --> 00:31:13,680
New arrivals, listen up.

350
00:31:14,560 --> 00:31:17,040
Take out your phones and turn them off.

351
00:31:17,120 --> 00:31:18,360
The guards will collect them.

352
00:31:19,920 --> 00:31:22,120
Only your bags and clothes

353
00:31:22,200 --> 00:31:24,520
are allowed inside.

354
00:31:24,600 --> 00:31:26,280
If anyone

355
00:31:26,360 --> 00:31:29,200
is caught hiding a phone,

356
00:31:29,280 --> 00:31:30,920
you will be severely punished.

357
00:31:32,200 --> 00:31:33,120
Hey.

358
00:31:34,520 --> 00:31:37,320
You said this was a job.
What kind of job is this?

359
00:31:37,400 --> 00:31:40,520
Why are you taking our phones?
This is my personal belonging.

360
00:31:40,600 --> 00:31:41,960
You've got a lot of attitude.

361
00:31:42,040 --> 00:31:43,320
Hey.

362
00:31:43,920 --> 00:31:44,760
Where are you taking me?

363
00:31:44,840 --> 00:31:46,720
-Let go!
-Come here!

364
00:31:54,160 --> 00:31:55,000
The rules here

365
00:31:55,800 --> 00:31:57,360
are as follows.

366
00:31:58,880 --> 00:32:02,520
No one here is allowed
to contact outsiders.

367
00:32:03,600 --> 00:32:04,520
No one is allowed to leave the building.

368
00:32:06,200 --> 00:32:09,560
We have everything here, a cafeteria,

369
00:32:09,640 --> 00:32:11,640
food, and all necessities.

370
00:32:11,720 --> 00:32:14,080
Everyone gets a salary of 25,000.

371
00:32:14,160 --> 00:32:18,160
If anyone earns more than 200,000 a month,
there's a commission bonus.

372
00:32:18,240 --> 00:32:20,840
Working hours are from 7 a.m.

373
00:32:20,920 --> 00:32:22,520
to 8 p.m. every day.

374
00:32:24,280 --> 00:32:27,800
You newcomers start tomorrow.

375
00:32:28,680 --> 00:32:30,800
Rest well tonight.

376
00:32:34,400 --> 00:32:36,640
So what's the job?

377
00:32:43,040 --> 00:32:44,200
Hello, sir.

378
00:32:46,120 --> 00:32:48,040
Your job

379
00:32:48,120 --> 00:32:50,080
is to randomly call customers.

380
00:32:54,760 --> 00:32:57,360
Do whatever it takes
to make them trust you

381
00:32:57,440 --> 00:33:00,840
and transfer money
into the account. Understand?

382
00:33:09,280 --> 00:33:12,240
<i>Let me keep you in my dreams</i>

383
00:33:15,320 --> 00:33:16,240
-Hey, Gao.
-Yeah?

384
00:33:16,320 --> 00:33:19,000
Don't you think this kind of life
is pretty good?

385
00:33:19,080 --> 00:33:23,440
Wake up, go out, drink, eat, sleep,

386
00:33:23,520 --> 00:33:26,160
and repeat. Feels amazing, right?

387
00:33:26,240 --> 00:33:30,040
-My friend.
-It's living and drinking to forget her.

388
00:33:30,120 --> 00:33:31,920
-Yeah, right.
-Hey.

389
00:33:32,000 --> 00:33:33,600
-Yeah.
-Fist bump.

390
00:33:33,680 --> 00:33:35,240
-Whose phone is that?
-Hey.

391
00:33:35,320 --> 00:33:36,680
It's mine.

392
00:33:37,760 --> 00:33:39,440
HONG

393
00:33:40,360 --> 00:33:44,680
Hey, Yak. Hong is calling again.
What should I do?

394
00:33:47,560 --> 00:33:48,760
Just hang up.

395
00:33:51,520 --> 00:33:52,360
Huh?

396
00:33:52,440 --> 00:33:53,440
What?

397
00:33:53,520 --> 00:33:57,520
I hope you're not going back
to get fooled by Hong again.

398
00:33:58,360 --> 00:34:01,600
Yak, when I say something, I mean it.

399
00:34:01,680 --> 00:34:02,640
She can call.

400
00:34:02,720 --> 00:34:05,120
I can just turn it off. That's it.

401
00:34:07,400 --> 00:34:08,239
What's next?

402
00:34:08,320 --> 00:34:10,480
What else? We're in Poipet.

403
00:34:10,560 --> 00:34:12,320
Of course, the casino.

404
00:34:15,719 --> 00:34:18,600
Win or lose, hope you win.

405
00:34:20,159 --> 00:34:22,400
Wow, acting all tough.

406
00:34:22,480 --> 00:34:24,679
Hello. Are you Thai?

407
00:34:24,760 --> 00:34:26,600
Oh, just came over for fun.

408
00:34:27,120 --> 00:34:29,639
-That was close.
-Yeah.

409
00:34:34,600 --> 00:34:37,440
Hey, Yak. Why aren't you following?

410
00:34:37,520 --> 00:34:38,800
What are you doing?

411
00:34:39,719 --> 00:34:41,880
-He looks familiar.
-Familiar what?

412
00:34:42,560 --> 00:34:43,880
Nothing. Let's go play some games.

413
00:34:52,360 --> 00:34:54,120
-Hello, Uncle.
-Captain.

414
00:34:54,199 --> 00:34:57,800
Have a seat. Have you eaten yet?
Order whatever you want.

415
00:34:57,880 --> 00:34:59,960
It's fine. Let's get straight to it.

416
00:35:01,400 --> 00:35:02,640
Does Louis come here often?

417
00:35:03,320 --> 00:35:06,760
Oh, quite often. He runs casinos here,

418
00:35:06,840 --> 00:35:08,760
hotels, and a lot of other businesses.

419
00:35:09,760 --> 00:35:11,280
How can I meet him?

420
00:35:11,960 --> 00:35:13,760
It's hard to get close to him, Captain.

421
00:35:14,800 --> 00:35:16,880
Why do you want to meet him anyway?

422
00:35:17,840 --> 00:35:19,320
A senior of mine…

423
00:35:20,200 --> 00:35:21,520
He had problems with him.

424
00:35:22,040 --> 00:35:24,720
I just want to know
whether Louis really took him.

425
00:35:24,800 --> 00:35:28,840
Well, anyone who messes with Louis
doesn't make it out.

426
00:35:30,080 --> 00:35:32,840
Even if they survive,
he still locks them up in a building

427
00:35:32,920 --> 00:35:34,320
out near the border.

428
00:35:36,440 --> 00:35:38,600
What building, Uncle?
Do you know where it is?

429
00:35:39,520 --> 00:35:41,440
Well, I'm not sure.

430
00:35:42,000 --> 00:35:45,160
I've heard it's a building
Louis uses as a call center.

431
00:35:45,760 --> 00:35:48,120
He also keeps people locked up there.

432
00:35:49,920 --> 00:35:52,840
Can you investigate for me?
Find out where that building is

433
00:35:52,920 --> 00:35:54,760
and whether my senior is really there.

434
00:35:56,600 --> 00:35:59,600
That's not easy, Captain.

435
00:36:05,520 --> 00:36:06,800
Here's the payment we agreed on.

436
00:36:09,520 --> 00:36:12,440
I'll give you more if you find him.

437
00:36:16,480 --> 00:36:17,760
By the way…

438
00:36:20,080 --> 00:36:21,800
What does your friend look like?

439
00:36:27,640 --> 00:36:30,040
Alright, send me this photo.

440
00:36:30,600 --> 00:36:33,280
But I can't promise I'll find him.

441
00:36:33,360 --> 00:36:37,240
But I'll report back
if there's any progress. Goodbye.

442
00:36:51,840 --> 00:36:53,600
SA KAEO 10 KM, KABINBURI 42 KM

443
00:37:09,360 --> 00:37:11,520
What do we do?
Risa hasn't turned her phone on.

444
00:37:11,600 --> 00:37:12,560
So what now?

445
00:37:12,640 --> 00:37:15,760
I wouldn't suggest
just crossing the border like that.

446
00:37:15,840 --> 00:37:17,000
You're right.

447
00:37:17,600 --> 00:37:19,480
If we try to cross legally,

448
00:37:19,560 --> 00:37:22,560
it's not a good idea either.
The police are after us right now.

449
00:37:23,240 --> 00:37:24,400
What do you want me to do?

450
00:37:24,480 --> 00:37:27,440
Just sit here and do nothing?
We know Risa is in danger.

451
00:37:27,520 --> 00:37:28,360
I can't do this.

452
00:37:28,440 --> 00:37:30,920
Hey, Mung. Mung!

453
00:37:33,600 --> 00:37:34,840
Chen, please.

454
00:37:36,360 --> 00:37:37,880
You have to call Koh now.

455
00:37:44,440 --> 00:37:45,840
What? What do you mean?

456
00:37:46,440 --> 00:37:49,880
Risa's in Poipet? Chen!

457
00:37:49,960 --> 00:37:53,520
<i>I told you to keep a close eye on her.</i>
<i>I can't trust you with anything, can I?</i>

458
00:37:54,120 --> 00:37:56,440
Hey, I'm sorry, man.

459
00:37:56,520 --> 00:37:59,920
I can't keep an eye on Risa
around the clock.

460
00:38:01,800 --> 00:38:05,160
You guys stay back. I'll handle it.
That's it.

461
00:38:05,240 --> 00:38:06,240
-Wait.
-Hey.

462
00:38:07,320 --> 00:38:09,880
We're already in Sa Kaeo.
You want us to go back? No way.

463
00:38:11,200 --> 00:38:12,160
Why did you all come?

464
00:38:13,000 --> 00:38:15,120
If you're not helping, fine.
We'll find our own way.

465
00:38:15,200 --> 00:38:17,200
-Hey.
-Mung, calm down.

466
00:38:17,720 --> 00:38:19,120
Koh.

467
00:38:20,040 --> 00:38:21,280
Risa's my dear friend.

468
00:38:22,160 --> 00:38:24,800
<i>If you expect me</i>
<i>to just stand by, I can't.</i>

469
00:38:27,720 --> 00:38:28,760
Exactly.

470
00:38:31,280 --> 00:38:34,880
We can lose anything,
but not our best friend.

471
00:38:39,160 --> 00:38:41,000
-Chen.
-Yeah?

472
00:38:41,640 --> 00:38:43,160
<i>Tell everyone to stay there.</i>

473
00:38:43,240 --> 00:38:45,720
Wait for a call
from someone named Uncle Au.

474
00:38:45,800 --> 00:38:49,000
I'll have him help you
cross through a back route.

475
00:38:49,080 --> 00:38:49,960
Then we'll figure the rest out.

476
00:38:50,040 --> 00:38:51,280
Okay.

477
00:38:53,680 --> 00:38:54,800
Yeah.

478
00:39:01,600 --> 00:39:04,000
Hello, Uncle Au. I need your help.

479
00:39:42,080 --> 00:39:42,920
Hey!

480
00:39:43,000 --> 00:39:45,840
Can you stop crying already?
I can't sleep.

481
00:39:46,560 --> 00:39:49,840
If I knew this was a scam call center,
I never would've applied.

482
00:39:51,000 --> 00:39:52,960
Crying won't change anything.

483
00:39:53,040 --> 00:39:55,280
They're not going to let you out anyway.

484
00:39:55,880 --> 00:39:58,480
Just endure it like I do.
Things will get better eventually.

485
00:40:00,840 --> 00:40:03,280
Hey, how long have you been here?

486
00:40:03,880 --> 00:40:04,920
Six months.

487
00:40:05,880 --> 00:40:07,320
Do you know someone named Louis?

488
00:40:07,920 --> 00:40:08,960
Which Louis? I don't know him.

489
00:40:09,600 --> 00:40:11,800
Can you stop asking so many questions?

490
00:40:11,880 --> 00:40:14,880
Just do what they tell you,
unless you want to get hurt.

491
00:40:20,440 --> 00:40:21,720
Get in.

492
00:40:22,360 --> 00:40:23,760
If you cause trouble again,

493
00:40:23,840 --> 00:40:26,680
I'll lock you up for good, you brat.

494
00:40:56,520 --> 00:40:57,360
What are you looking at?

495
00:40:58,680 --> 00:40:59,680
Can't I look?

496
00:41:02,320 --> 00:41:05,080
You're new here. Know your place.

497
00:41:27,560 --> 00:41:28,560
Here.

498
00:41:31,760 --> 00:41:34,680
New here? Fried rice is 150 baht.
Noodles are 200.

499
00:41:35,840 --> 00:41:39,120
Fried rice is 150? Seriously?

500
00:41:39,200 --> 00:41:40,880
Are you eating or not?

501
00:41:43,560 --> 00:41:44,720
How much are the cup noodles?

502
00:41:44,800 --> 00:41:46,360
A hundred. Hot water's free.

503
00:41:51,440 --> 00:41:52,480
Here.

504
00:41:52,560 --> 00:41:54,520
One cup of noodles, Auntie.

505
00:41:56,640 --> 00:42:00,080
Want some meatballs too, kid?
I'll give them to you for free.

506
00:42:01,720 --> 00:42:02,840
Thank you.

507
00:42:07,400 --> 00:42:10,200
Hey, it's all the same price.
Why'd you give her free meatballs?

508
00:42:10,280 --> 00:42:12,120
I can give them to whoever I want.

509
00:42:13,160 --> 00:42:16,000
Alright, here you go.

510
00:42:19,440 --> 00:42:20,280
Hey.

511
00:42:20,360 --> 00:42:22,520
Don't mess with that brat.

512
00:42:22,600 --> 00:42:24,400
-What would you like?
-Why not?

513
00:42:24,920 --> 00:42:29,000
That girl doesn't respect anyone.
She thinks she's been here the longest,

514
00:42:29,080 --> 00:42:31,840
so she acts tough
and talks trash to everybody.

515
00:42:31,920 --> 00:42:33,320
Is she some big shot around here?

516
00:42:34,440 --> 00:42:38,000
Not really. She just hits her targets.

517
00:42:38,080 --> 00:42:39,560
That's why the guards like her.

518
00:42:39,640 --> 00:42:42,200
But nobody here likes her.

519
00:42:43,440 --> 00:42:45,960
See this? She did it. The other day,

520
00:42:46,040 --> 00:42:49,160
she stabbed my hand with a fork.
She thought she'd get away with it,

521
00:42:49,680 --> 00:42:52,160
but in the end, she got locked up.

522
00:42:53,240 --> 00:42:54,440
Serves her right.

523
00:42:57,320 --> 00:43:00,160
-Is it ready yet?
-Hold on. I forgot.

524
00:43:03,920 --> 00:43:04,880
Here.

525
00:43:17,760 --> 00:43:18,800
Pao.

526
00:43:20,400 --> 00:43:24,080
Pao, it's almost noon.
How much longer are you going to sleep?

527
00:43:24,640 --> 00:43:26,520
Wake up, Pao.

528
00:43:31,280 --> 00:43:34,880
We walked through the forest all night.
Can I sleep a little longer?

529
00:43:36,640 --> 00:43:38,480
I'll give you five minutes, okay?

530
00:43:39,040 --> 00:43:41,520
Once Sis Hong comes out
of the bathroom, get up.

531
00:43:46,360 --> 00:43:49,000
Hey, did you bring the communication gear?

532
00:43:50,280 --> 00:43:52,200
-Huh? Did you bring it?
-Yeah.

533
00:43:55,240 --> 00:43:56,240
What about the bugging device?

534
00:43:56,320 --> 00:43:58,160
I brought it.

535
00:43:58,680 --> 00:43:59,840
Geez.

536
00:43:59,920 --> 00:44:01,680
Did you bring the laptop and power bank?

537
00:44:02,280 --> 00:44:03,920
-Pao!
-Ugh!

538
00:44:07,240 --> 00:44:08,960
What? Just answer me.

539
00:44:14,120 --> 00:44:15,800
Here.

540
00:44:15,880 --> 00:44:18,160
Everything's in here.

541
00:44:20,760 --> 00:44:23,960
If you want to check something, go ahead.
I'm going back to sleep.

542
00:44:24,040 --> 00:44:25,680
Please don't ask me anything else.

543
00:44:27,560 --> 00:44:30,000
-Hey, good news.
-Chen.

544
00:44:30,080 --> 00:44:31,000
-Yeah?
-Did you find a rental car?

545
00:44:31,080 --> 00:44:32,440
Yeah, I got one.

546
00:44:32,520 --> 00:44:34,760
Now we're just waiting for Koh's contact

547
00:44:34,840 --> 00:44:37,640
to call and tell us
where the Hyena Group call center is.

548
00:44:37,720 --> 00:44:40,080
Then we'll go in and rescue Risa.

549
00:44:40,680 --> 00:44:41,880
-Okay.
-Yeah.

550
00:44:41,960 --> 00:44:42,880
Here it is.

551
00:44:44,600 --> 00:44:45,720
He's calling.

552
00:44:46,320 --> 00:44:48,640
Hello. Is this Mr. Au?

553
00:44:51,640 --> 00:44:53,240
-Who?
-I don't know.

554
00:44:54,280 --> 00:44:55,560
Hello.

555
00:44:55,640 --> 00:44:57,080
<i>This is Thailand Post.</i>

556
00:44:57,160 --> 00:44:59,920
<i>You have an unclaimed parcel</i>
<i>in Chiang Mai that's been pending</i>

557
00:45:00,000 --> 00:45:03,280
<i>for over a month.</i>
<i>Please contact our office.</i>

558
00:45:03,360 --> 00:45:07,240
Sorry, I'm in Bangkok.
I never ordered anything to Chiang Mai.

559
00:45:07,320 --> 00:45:10,200
I don't even shop online.
How could I have a parcel there?

560
00:45:10,280 --> 00:45:11,520
Bro.

561
00:45:12,280 --> 00:45:13,800
It's a scam call center.

562
00:45:14,560 --> 00:45:16,400
They trick people into sending money.

563
00:45:17,080 --> 00:45:18,520
Haven't you seen the news?

564
00:45:22,400 --> 00:45:23,240
<i>Hello?</i>

565
00:45:24,880 --> 00:45:26,520
<i>Hello.</i>

566
00:45:26,600 --> 00:45:27,520
Hello.

567
00:45:28,120 --> 00:45:30,840
May I ask who's speaking?

568
00:45:30,920 --> 00:45:32,040
I'm--

569
00:45:33,880 --> 00:45:37,200
My name is Sandon Nonsense.

570
00:45:37,280 --> 00:45:40,160
Sorry about that. My nephew
was using the phone earlier

571
00:45:42,680 --> 00:45:43,840
<i>Yes, Mr. Sandon.</i>

572
00:45:43,920 --> 00:45:47,720
You have an unclaimed parcel
at the Chiang Mai Post Office.

573
00:45:49,120 --> 00:45:50,240
<i>Really?</i>

574
00:45:50,320 --> 00:45:51,960
How did that happen?

575
00:45:52,920 --> 00:45:56,960
The police suspect
it may contain illegal items.

576
00:46:00,120 --> 00:46:03,600
Your name has now appeared
on a list of persons under investigation.

577
00:46:04,200 --> 00:46:07,160
I'll transfer your call to the police.

578
00:46:07,840 --> 00:46:10,160
Yeah, but before you do,

579
00:46:10,240 --> 00:46:11,600
can I ask you something?

580
00:46:12,200 --> 00:46:15,160
-Yes.
-Do you really believe

581
00:46:15,240 --> 00:46:18,800
there's a person in this world
named Sandon Nonsense?

582
00:46:21,240 --> 00:46:22,360
What?

583
00:46:22,440 --> 00:46:24,680
Why don't you get an honest job

584
00:46:24,760 --> 00:46:26,840
instead of scamming people like this?

585
00:46:26,920 --> 00:46:29,400
Go scam your own father.
Take every last penny he's got.

586
00:46:29,480 --> 00:46:31,560
Watch how much he suffers.

587
00:46:31,640 --> 00:46:32,920
Maybe you'll learn some empathy,
you psycho.

588
00:46:37,080 --> 00:46:37,960
Here.

589
00:46:38,600 --> 00:46:39,440
Can I sleep now?

590
00:46:41,040 --> 00:46:42,800
What kind of stupid script is this?

591
00:46:42,880 --> 00:46:44,840
I follow the script
and still get insulted.

592
00:46:44,920 --> 00:46:46,640
I'm losing my mind!

593
00:46:47,480 --> 00:46:48,760
What the hell is wrong with you?

594
00:46:49,960 --> 00:46:51,840
What's wrong with you? What's wrong?

595
00:46:56,200 --> 00:46:57,120
You looking at me?

596
00:46:58,120 --> 00:47:01,200
Pick it up and keep calling.

597
00:47:01,280 --> 00:47:02,520
Now! Hurry up!

598
00:47:05,320 --> 00:47:06,360
PICHET - INCOMING VIDEO CALL

599
00:47:07,240 --> 00:47:08,800
Hey, stop!

600
00:47:09,560 --> 00:47:11,600
That idiot is video-calling Oab again.

601
00:47:12,440 --> 00:47:14,240
Last time he transferred 400,000 baht.

602
00:47:14,320 --> 00:47:15,840
Now he's calling again?

603
00:47:19,040 --> 00:47:20,600
Answer it, but don't turn on the camera.

604
00:47:24,440 --> 00:47:26,200
JOIN WITHOUT CAMERA

605
00:47:29,120 --> 00:47:30,480
Hello.

606
00:47:30,560 --> 00:47:31,520
<i>Som.</i>

607
00:47:32,440 --> 00:47:35,000
<i>Please send my money back.</i>

608
00:47:36,000 --> 00:47:38,640
<i>Som, the truth is, that money</i>

609
00:47:38,720 --> 00:47:40,000
<i>isn't mine.</i>

610
00:47:40,080 --> 00:47:42,560
<i>I secretly took it from my company</i>

611
00:47:42,640 --> 00:47:44,200
<i>and transferred it to you.</i>

612
00:47:44,280 --> 00:47:46,640
<i>If you don't send it back today,</i>

613
00:47:46,720 --> 00:47:49,760
<i>the company will find out,</i>
<i>and I'll get arrested.</i>

614
00:47:53,960 --> 00:47:55,720
Chet.

615
00:47:55,800 --> 00:47:58,560
I really can't return the money right now.

616
00:47:58,640 --> 00:48:00,040
<i>Why not, Som?</i>

617
00:48:05,880 --> 00:48:07,200
Speak.

618
00:48:12,240 --> 00:48:15,760
Actually, there is a way
to withdraw your investment funds.

619
00:48:17,080 --> 00:48:17,920
<i>How, Som?</i>

620
00:48:18,440 --> 00:48:21,480
You just need to add a security deposit.

621
00:48:22,320 --> 00:48:26,040
But don't worry. You'll definitely
get the full amount back.

622
00:48:27,880 --> 00:48:29,120
How much?

623
00:48:33,720 --> 00:48:35,040
Another 50,000 baht, Chet.

624
00:48:42,880 --> 00:48:43,720
Hey.

625
00:48:44,240 --> 00:48:45,440
<i>How many more lives</i>
<i>are you going to ruin before you stop?</i>

626
00:48:46,240 --> 00:48:48,120
<i>You're a call center scammer, aren't you?</i>

627
00:48:48,200 --> 00:48:49,080
Aren't you?

628
00:48:50,640 --> 00:48:52,440
<i>Why are you doing this to me?</i>

629
00:48:53,280 --> 00:48:56,440
You tricked me. You ruined my life.

630
00:48:56,520 --> 00:48:57,880
<i>I've got nothing left!</i>

631
00:49:10,600 --> 00:49:13,760
<i>Som, I'm begging you.</i>

632
00:49:16,560 --> 00:49:18,440
I'm begging you for the last time.

633
00:49:20,080 --> 00:49:21,200
<i>Please send</i>

634
00:49:22,320 --> 00:49:24,640
the money back. Please, Som.

635
00:49:25,640 --> 00:49:26,560
I'm begging you.

636
00:49:58,560 --> 00:50:00,760
Can't be helped.
It's his own fault for being stupid.

637
00:50:07,560 --> 00:50:09,920
Why are you just sitting there?
Get back to work!

638
00:50:10,000 --> 00:50:11,520
You looking for trouble?

639
00:50:22,080 --> 00:50:24,720
Sir, I need to use the bathroom.

640
00:51:43,880 --> 00:51:44,760
Dad.

641
00:51:45,760 --> 00:51:47,480
I can't do this anymore.

642
00:51:49,320 --> 00:51:51,640
I don't want to do this anymore, Dad.

643
00:51:52,400 --> 00:51:53,800
I want to go home.

644
00:51:54,880 --> 00:51:57,360
Can you get me out of here?

645
00:51:58,040 --> 00:52:02,120
Or tell someone to come get me?

646
00:52:09,480 --> 00:52:10,800
Yes, Dad.

647
00:52:12,200 --> 00:52:13,600
I'll hang in there.

648
00:52:59,080 --> 00:53:02,040
Hyena Group has two call center compounds.

649
00:53:02,600 --> 00:53:04,840
One is near the edge of the forest,

650
00:53:04,920 --> 00:53:07,040
and the other
is about 15 kilometers deeper inside.

651
00:53:07,120 --> 00:53:08,680
What time do they finish work?

652
00:53:08,760 --> 00:53:10,560
Around 8 p.m.

653
00:53:10,640 --> 00:53:13,080
After that, they turn off the lights
and make everyone go to sleep.

654
00:53:13,160 --> 00:53:15,320
Good. Then that's when we'll go in.

655
00:53:15,400 --> 00:53:17,320
Hey, don't forget.

656
00:53:17,400 --> 00:53:19,840
That's also when the guards
start their shift.

657
00:53:20,720 --> 00:53:22,080
Can we go in a little later?

658
00:53:23,400 --> 00:53:26,760
Alright. Which compound
are you hitting first?

659
00:53:27,360 --> 00:53:30,240
I suggest starting
with the one near the forest edge.

660
00:53:30,320 --> 00:53:32,840
If we don't find them there,
then we'll move on to the other one.

661
00:53:32,920 --> 00:53:34,120
No.

662
00:53:35,200 --> 00:53:36,880
We're hitting both compounds
at the same time.

663
00:53:38,320 --> 00:53:40,120
How is that possible? I'm alone.

664
00:53:40,200 --> 00:53:42,240
How am I supposed
to take you to two places at once?

665
00:53:51,960 --> 00:53:52,880
Hey, wait.

666
00:53:57,320 --> 00:53:58,600
Why hit both compounds at the same time?

667
00:53:59,400 --> 00:54:02,400
Think ahead. If one team fails,
the other can still get through.

668
00:54:02,480 --> 00:54:05,120
If we get caught at the first compound,

669
00:54:05,200 --> 00:54:06,800
how are we supposed
to make it to the second?

670
00:54:07,800 --> 00:54:11,240
More importantly, if they figure out
who we're looking for,

671
00:54:11,840 --> 00:54:13,280
what do you think they'll do to Risa?

672
00:54:15,640 --> 00:54:19,080
I'm not letting anything happen to Risa.

673
00:54:44,640 --> 00:54:45,720
What do you want?

674
00:55:07,880 --> 00:55:11,000
Tonight, Oab is definitely in trouble.

675
00:55:11,080 --> 00:55:12,240
Why?

676
00:55:12,320 --> 00:55:15,120
I saw her take a phone
out of the call room.

677
00:55:15,720 --> 00:55:18,520
I'll report her, so the guards
come for her tonight.

678
00:55:19,520 --> 00:55:22,280
This time, she's really screwed.

679
00:55:37,720 --> 00:55:38,640
I saw it with my own eyes.

680
00:55:38,720 --> 00:55:41,680
Oab secretly took a phone
out of the call room.

681
00:55:42,800 --> 00:55:45,080
Do you think she hid it in her room?

682
00:55:45,680 --> 00:55:49,480
I didn't see that.
You should go up and search her room.

683
00:55:50,320 --> 00:55:53,760
And the last time you saw her,
where do you think

684
00:55:53,840 --> 00:55:55,240
she might've hidden it?

685
00:56:01,240 --> 00:56:03,600
<i>I don't know what you're planning,</i>

686
00:56:04,240 --> 00:56:06,240
<i>but you shouldn't go down there.</i>

687
00:56:06,320 --> 00:56:07,640
Took you long enough, Koh.

688
00:56:07,720 --> 00:56:09,040
I've been waiting for you.

689
00:56:09,120 --> 00:56:10,520
Run, you guys! It's a trap!

690
00:56:10,600 --> 00:56:11,920
Huh?

691
00:56:12,000 --> 00:56:13,480
I think he's been betrayed.

692
00:56:13,560 --> 00:56:15,680
<i>We know you came to Poipet</i>
<i>looking for your dad.</i>

693
00:56:15,760 --> 00:56:17,400
<i>Koh's been captured.</i>

694
00:56:17,480 --> 00:56:19,720
<i>Don't do anything reckless.</i>

695
00:56:19,800 --> 00:56:21,200
We're figuring out a way to get inside.

696
00:56:21,280 --> 00:56:22,680
<i>There are way too many of them.</i>

697
00:56:22,760 --> 00:56:23,840
How are they supposed to get out?

698
00:56:23,920 --> 00:56:25,000
<i>Can you tell Mungkorn</i>

699
00:56:25,080 --> 00:56:27,200
<i>to wait until tonight?</i>
<i>It'll be safer to escape then.</i>

700
00:56:27,280 --> 00:56:29,160
<i>If we wait that long,</i>
<i>my friends won't make it.</i>

701
00:56:29,240 --> 00:56:30,560
Angpao!

702
00:56:32,080 --> 00:56:33,480
Run!

703
00:56:34,280 --> 00:56:35,360
Come on!

704
00:56:36,320 --> 00:56:37,200
You guys…

705
00:56:40,040 --> 00:56:40,920
Uncle!

706
00:57:27,080 --> 00:57:31,280
Subtitle translation by:
Chomchanach Yanaharn
